n polls show.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Andy Ogles (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Tennessee's 5th District is an open Republican-held seat after Andy Ogles lost renomination, with state Agriculture Commissioner Charlie Hatcher carrying the GOP banner against Democrat Chaz Molder. The district's R+10 lean and a national environment favoring Republicans form the core of the race's structure, and every major rating outlet calls it Safe or Solid Republican.\n\nMolder has out-raised Hatcher by roughly two to one and has more cash on hand, and the race has drawn genuine local attention with candidate forums across the district. But the only polls, conducted by a Democratic-leaning firm, still show Hatcher ahead by five to eight points, and markets price Molder's chances at under ten percent. The seat remains very likely to stay Republican, with Molder needing an unusually strong late break to close a structural gap.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.079, "margin": -8.8}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0675, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0985, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0839, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0593, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0597, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0699, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0949, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0595, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0915, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0612, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0794, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.1021, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0644, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.0751, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.0564, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.1019, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.1538, "margin": -6